/** @page ncursesreleasenotes Release Notes

    @section ncurses_1_0 ncurses Module Version 1.0
    - initial release

    Reusable EditorAssistance, BackgroundTask and Dialogs controllers own popup/focus
    cleanup, worker result delivery and adaptive confirmation/prompt/file workflows.
    NcursesQore provides an optional language adapter using a caller's live QoreRepl
    session. StatusBarWidget supports priority and compact labels; PanelWidget supports
    clamped centered sizing, and FormWidget supports application-specific action labels.
    qrepl adopts these APIs for syntax highlighting, exact completion ranges, help,
    real file selection/save prompts, consistent quitting and responsive evaluation.
    Output streams during work and edits made during evaluation survive its result.
    Capture preserves inherited output handles even after a runner drops privileges.
    EditorBuffer::setHistory() can preserve an active history-browsing snapshot and
    unfinished draft during background updates; qrepl uses this when evaluation completes.
    The backend does not expose safe cancellation; quit can wait for completion.
    Five full-application stories exercise the actual qrepl code through its event loop.

    ProgressWidget uses semantic state colors, emphasized fill/counts and focused
    actions while retaining plain-text inspection. TableWidget headers use bold
    underlining, distinct from reverse-video data selection in color and monochrome.
    TextChartWidget now defaults to Unicode sparklines with explicit min/max and gap
    legends. setUnicode(False) retains an ASCII fallback; setChartHeight(6) enables
    larger bars with six rows of resolution. TextChart::bars() returns expanded
    plain-text charts; the existing sparkline() string API remains ASCII by default.
    Chart presentation updates retain the scrolled reading position; replacing the
    data snapshot explicitly returns to its summary.

    FormWidget now groups bold field labels, descriptions and validation messages
    above visibly bounded values, with spacing between fields and a non-color focus
    marker. Clicking a label, description or error focuses its value without changing
    it; read-only, disabled and detached fields cannot acquire focus this way.
    Application-disabled controls remain disabled across model synchronization and
    submission transitions. Metadata clicks lay out pending errors or replacement
    fields even when focus does not change.
    Compact layout preserves the field label and input when at least two rows are
    available, marks truncated metadata with an ellipsis, and restores it after resize.
    Existing field/control APIs and typed drafts are preserved; applications with
    fixed mouse coordinates or field-row assumptions must use the new control frames.

    Interactive UX follow-up adds continuous WebGL box drawing to Storybook, explicit
    compact/stress/recovery scenarios, live action/state feedback and a code editor
    story using astparser syntax highlighting and qrepl completion/signature hints.
    Default labels use ordinary text; Unicode stress cases remain explicitly named.
    DescribedChoiceWidget separates bold focused titles, indented descriptions,
    recommendations and selection marks. Its default story permits repeated selection;
    a separate submission story explains its one-shot lifecycle.
    ButtonWidget paints primary-press feedback and activates on release inside the
    original target; outside release, focus loss, resize, detachment and modal changes
    cancel the press. Keyboard/synthesized clicks remain immediate. Window::readEvent()
    drains native mouse events queued behind one KEY_MOUSE notification before the next
    key; rapid press/release gestures no longer lose their release. flushInput() also
    clears the separate mouse queue. EventDispatcher
    owns scoped mouse capture and cleans it up on errors.
    FileBrowserWidget shows one full-width pane below 48 content columns; F7 switches
    panes while retaining selection. Unselected previews provide guidance and empty
    files are identified from bounded reads rather than metadata size alone; special
    files are not read for previews. Assistance popups release their panels on outside
    primary clicks before forwarding input, and dismiss when resize or clipping
    removes their caret anchor so hidden modal scopes cannot trap editing.
    Application::removeModal() and EventDispatcher::removeModal() remove scopes
    by widget identity, including beneath another overlay, preserving active focus,
    mouse capture and the surviving overlays' focus-restoration chain.
    Top-scope cleanup also completes when a mouse-capture-loss callback throws;
    the original failure propagates after attempting focus restoration.
    Code completion replaces the full token
    around the caret and preserves existing call parentheses and namespace separators,
    including intervening spaces, tabs and line breaks. Compact dialogs prioritize the wrapped message
    over decorative padding while retaining actions.
    PanelWidget::setBorderEdges() supports independent edges; content padding is now
    additional to border insets and is preserved when borders change. Existing default
    panel content insets remain one cell. Full-width gallery panels omit side borders.
    TextEditorWidget::setHighlighter() applies source-preserving ANSI styles without
    changing editing offsets or undo; providers run on the UI thread and errors retain
    drafts. TerminalText::styledLines() preserves ANSI styles over hard newlines.

    Storybook now reviews the actual native gallery through a local PTY/xterm.js
    adapter. Shared keyboard, mouse, background-output and cancellation scenarios
    produce composed cell/cursor/focus/scroll evidence and exact PNG comparisons.
    Baselines require explicit recorded review; the existing Ubuntu CI job publishes
    baseline/current/diff artifacts and preserves successful-tree reuse.
    The gallery reconciles nonmodal cursor visibility after state and focus changes,
    hiding stale editing carets on disabled fields and non-editing controls.

    Mouse review fixes restrict button and checkbox activation to their visible
    complete painted label graphemes, including narrow Unicode clipping. They dim
    disabled checkboxes, recognize terminal Enter variants, and map attachment actions through normalized,
    wrapped and scrolled text. Completion popups support primary-click selection,
    wheel navigation, double-click acceptance and consistent Enter handling.
    Timeline selection and file-selection toggles accept real terminal press/release
    input as well as synthesized clicks, without repeating an action on release.
    FileBrowserWidget exposes F7 pane switching for keyboard-only preview access,
    retaining Tab/Shift+Tab directory navigation and showing the binding in its help.

    Session::capture() adds typed, serializable physical-screen frames with panel
    composition, Unicode leading/continuation cells, attributes, palette colors and
    cursor state. It observes completed output without changing live drawing state.
    Session::resize() applies known terminal geometry synchronously for deterministic
    layout and capture checkpoints. Session::terminalSize() reads device dimensions
    independently of logical viewport presets. The existing base-window snapshot() API is preserved.

    A shared executable story registry supplies the generated widget catalog, searchable
    native gallery and headless state/interaction checks for all 27 concrete widgets.
    Gallery controls provide direct selection, reset, contextual help, viewport presets
    and focus/scroll/cursor inspection. Session::updatePanels() stages base-only output
    when no native panel is visible, fixing blank terminal frames before libpanel initializes
    its screen hook while retaining its overlap propagation when panels are present. TableWidget::getScrollOffset() exposes
    the first visible data row for inspection and behavioral assertions;
    AssistancePopupWidget::getSelectedResult() exposes the selected result metadata.

    Scrollable text prepares wrapping before measuring scroll limits, maps
    source positions to display cells, preserves the viewport anchor on resize,
    and clips styled Unicode text at widget boundaries. Cursor requests can be
    released without disturbing a newer request from another widget. Develop
    pipelines reuse successful platform tests for identical Git trees.

    Focus routing reaches nested controls, modal scopes preserve Tab traversal
    and restore eligible prior focus, and explicit popups support outside-click
    dismissal. Text inputs and combo boxes share grapheme-safe editing and mouse
    caret mapping. Cursor indices remain character offsets; partial replacement
    ranges expand to whole graphemes. Session::setCursor() now returns the prior
    visibility so modal transitions can restore it exactly. Bound form controls
    synchronize pending model writes before all input dispatch. Composite file-browser
    pane navigation stays synchronized with managed focus, and combo-box mouse
    placement and dropdown scrolling share the clipped drawing geometry.
    Composite mouse delegation preserves preview navigation. Focus callbacks share a thread-local transition guard,
    including cleanup triggered by hiding, disabling, and detaching widgets.
    Modal initialization rolls back if a focus callback makes its root
    unavailable, and file-browser keyboard delegation excludes unavailable panes.
    Outside primary clicks, including double and triple clicks, close menu panels
    and release menu state before forwarding the event to the underlying control.

    Panel children now share the screen-coordinate layout/input contract and
    convert drawing to window-local coordinates. Clipped inputs keep the caret
    visible at the right edge; panel windows accept focused child cursor requests.
    Derived native windows retain their parents, preventing shared-storage leaks
    when the parent wrapper is released first. Panel replacement preserves the
    old resources on creation failure. Box layouts constrain overflowing requests,
    and active dialogs and anchored popups reflow on resize. Tiny dialogs expose
    every action through keyboard navigation and scroll wrapped messages.

    Tables add stable identity across refreshes, numeric/date/string/custom
    sorting, filtering, horizontal column navigation, row actions, primary mouse
    selection, double-click activation and wheel navigation. Equal sort keys are
    stable; invalid data/comparator failures preserve the preceding view.
    Radio groups, menus and combo boxes keep active choices visible using actual
    drawable rows, support page/home/end and mouse navigation, and clear obsolete
    rows. Disabled-only menus no longer risk an unbounded navigation loop.
    Nested panels retain logical geometry and open intent independently of clipped
    native resources, including full clipping and later regrowth. Hit testing
    follows ancestor clipping; left-clipped lists, checkboxes, menus and status
    bars render their visible suffixes. Table column selection stays visible after
    resize, and empty row hashes remain valid selections for actions and activation.

    TextEditorWidget adds hard newlines, soft wrapping, styled prompts, preferred
    visual columns, bounded height, selection, clipboard hooks, undo/redo and
    searchable history that restores unfinished drafts. Bracketed paste arrives
    as a bounded Paste event, with fragmented input, cancellation and oversized
    payload recovery. Native and injected Alt input preserve Unicode characters.
    Synthetic event batches now commit atomically into a bounded module queue;
    overflow leaves previously queued input intact.

    TranscriptWidget adds stable source identities, logical blocks, incremental
    streaming updates, retention, search/highlights, selection/copy, collapse and
    link callbacks. Manual scrolling pauses following and tracks unread output.
    Indexed line extents and two cached wrap widths avoid rewrapping old text on
    appends/edits. InputBuffer caches grapheme positions. Dirty drawing preserves
    overlapping siblings, exposed regions and modal overlays while skipping idle
    frames. Width-aware box measurement sizes wrapped editors before allocation.

    qrepl uses separate transcript and draft viewports, retains failed drafts,
    exposes output/history search and internal clipboard bindings, and anchors
    completion to the wrapped caret. Ordinary Enter is normalized without changing
    literal paste or Alt input. Clipped subtree invalidation, clean panel removal,
    transcript mouse anchors, scrollbar following and collapse source text are covered
    by regressions. Its capture worker uses explicit flush and
    shutdown acknowledgement, preserves blank lines and split UTF-8, and reports
    invalid output bytes without sending malformed strings to the renderer.

    FormModel/FormWidget add typed metadata, field/form validation, inline errors,
    draft-preserving submission, cancellation generations and first-error focus.
    LabelWidget, ButtonWidget and DescribedChoiceWidget provide wrapped help, guarded
    actions, stable described choices, defaults/disabled options and custom responses.
    TextInputWidget supports password masking, safe paste and failed-submit rollback.
    TreeWidget/KeyValueWidget provide bounded iterative typed inspection, stable paths,
    filtering, expansion and copy/export callbacks. CodeViewWidget adds source-preserving
    export and validated syntax styling. Oversized ANSI parameters no longer overflow
    into unrelated styles; parsing and style scans support cooperative cancellation.
    Further repaint/navigation regressions restore exposed non-panel modal regions,
    retain invalidation after failed forced paints, acknowledge tiny file-browser panes,
    retain collapsed scroll anchors, reset stale preferred caret columns, reveal search
    matches horizontally and use actual window bounds for first-paint tail following.
    Password submission mode changes cannot leak submitted secrets into history, and
    failed submissions restore masking. Form focus scrolling honors ancestor and target-window clipping.
    Forms preserve unset Boolean values until an explicit edit and reveal completed submission receipts.
    Tree indentation and branch hit testing use the effective clipped viewport width.
    Failed form submissions preserve externally updated values, code replacement resets both scroll axes,
    custom choice carets preserve manual scrolling, and tree rebuilds notify selected-entry changes.
    Present validator errors, including empty/numeric strings, always prevent submission.
    Numeric text identities remain valid, and incomplete field/choice metadata is rejected atomically.
    AssistanceModel and AssistancePopupWidget add ranked/filterable completion,
    precise grapheme-aligned replacement ranges, diagnostic navigation, signature
    help, documented suggestions and guarded actions. Request identity, generation
    and editor revision reject stale results; provider errors preserve editing.

    ActionModel, ProgressWidget and TimelineWidget provide explicit operation states,
    determinate/unknown-total progress, timestamped expandable history, cancellation,
    retry and receipts. They compose with described choices for keyboard review actions.
    UiEventQueue/UiEventScope deliver bounded FIFO worker data on the UI thread,
    dispose hidden/disabled/detached owners, and release captures outside queue locks.
    Application integrates event delivery, removable owned tick callbacks and native
    wake notifications. Idle readEvent() waits release the ncurses lock, cancellation
    interrupts them, and Session::wakeup() coalesces work without synthesizing input.
    Only one input reader may be active per session; fork children isolate wake pipes.

    FileSelectionModel/Widget add stable single/multiple selections, filtering,
    hidden/unavailable selection summaries, local-path validation and application-owned
    open/save/export callbacks. AttachmentWidget presents metadata, text/chart previews
    and explicit unsupported-media fallbacks. TextChart/TextChartWidget offer numeric
    summaries and ASCII or optional Unicode sparklines with gaps and finite-data checks.
    List navigation uses the clipped viewport while retaining left-clipped text suffixes;
    combined double-click masks activate correctly. Progress bars fit their first paint
    even when content creates a scrollbar. Executable examples exercise real worker
    delivery, review actions, precise assistance edits and file/media controls.
*/
